Lecture Notes
=============

These are lecture notes transcribed while I was a PhD student. They were
originally intended as source material for two books with Paul Loya, but they
remain working notes rather than a published text.

Main sources
------------

* `Lecture draft/Lecture draft.tex` -- b-calculus, APS theory, and related
  analytic material.
* `Lecture draft/Atiyah-Singer index theorem.tex` -- Dirac operators, heat
  kernels, Clifford modules, characteristic classes, and the index theorem.
* `Lecture draft/Chapter 11.tex` -- a stand-alone extract from the first set of
  notes.

Building
--------

Run the builds from `Lecture draft/` so that the image paths resolve:

```
latexmk -pdf "Lecture draft.tex"
latexmk -pdf "Atiyah-Singer index theorem.tex"
```

Both main sources compile with pdfLaTeX. Generated PDFs and some historical
build artifacts are retained because they were part of the original archive.

Editorial status
----------------

The July 2026 audit repaired several substantive gaps in the heat-calculus,
Clifford-algebra, Dolbeault, and eta-invariant discussions and restored clean
builds. The manuscripts are large historical transcriptions, however, and
still contain informal lecture commentary, typographical errors, and claims
that have not received a line-by-line mathematical audit. Cite a standard
reference for any result used in research.
